menu "Waveshare Knob-Touch-LCD-1.8 board"

comment "Display"

config WSKNOB_LCD_BGR
    bool "Panel expects BGR element order"
    default n
    help
      Swaps red and blue. Waveshare's demo drives the panel as RGB, which
      is what n gives. Check against a deliberate red/green/blue test
      pattern, not a screen of UI chrome, which will not show a swap.

config WSKNOB_LCD_MIRROR_X
    bool "Mirror the display horizontally"
    default n
    help
      Waveshare's demo draws upright with no mirroring (MADCTL 0x00), and
      so does this firmware. Set this if text reads backwards.

config WSKNOB_LCD_MIRROR_Y
    bool "Mirror the display vertically"
    default n
    help
      To turn the picture upside down, set WSKNOB_ROTATE_180 rather than
      changing the mirrors.

config WSKNOB_ROTATE_180
    bool "Module is mounted rotated 180 degrees"
    default n
    help
      Turns the picture and the on-screen ring round by 180 degrees, so the
      face reads upright and ring patterns still point where the head unit
      drew them. The knob and the touch need nothing: turning the module in
      its own plane keeps clockwise clockwise.

comment "Knob"

config WSKNOB_KNOB_INVERT
    bool "Invert rotation direction"
    default n
    help
      Clockwise must increase. As wired, EC1_A (GPIO8) closes on a clockwise
      step and EC1_B (GPIO7) on an anticlockwise one, the way Waveshare's
      encoder demo counts them. Set this if the head unit sees the knob
      going the wrong way.

config WSKNOB_KNOB_DEBUG
    bool "Log each detent reported"
    default n

comment "Touch"

config WSKNOB_TOUCH_DEBUG
    bool "Log each touch down and up"
    default n

comment "Haptics"

config WSKNOB_HAPTIC
    bool "Use the vibration motor"
    default y
    help
      The screen is this dial's select button and has no travel, so the
      DRV2605 plays a short effect on every touch down to stand in for the
      click of a switch. The head unit does not know; it only sees down/up.
      The motor also plays the head unit's turn ticks
      (WSKNOB_HAPTIC_TURN).

choice WSKNOB_HAPTIC_MOTOR
    prompt "Motor type"
    default WSKNOB_HAPTIC_MOTOR_ERM
    depends on WSKNOB_HAPTIC
    help
      How the DRV2605 drives the motor. Waveshare's demo sets it up as an
      ERM in open loop with effect library 5, and that is the default. The
      schematic names the motor's nets LRA_P/LRA_N; if the clicks feel
      weak, try the LRA setting.

config WSKNOB_HAPTIC_MOTOR_ERM
    bool "ERM, open loop, library 5 (as Waveshare's demo)"

config WSKNOB_HAPTIC_MOTOR_LRA
    bool "LRA, closed loop, library 6"

endchoice

config WSKNOB_HAPTIC_EFFECT
    int "DRV2605 library effect played on touch (1-123)"
    range 1 123
    default 1
    depends on WSKNOB_HAPTIC
    help
      From the DRV2605 datasheet's waveform library: 1 strong click 100%,
      4 sharp click 100%, 7 soft bump 100%, 24 sharp tick 100%, 10 double
      click 100%.

config WSKNOB_HAPTIC_TURN
    bool "Tick the motor as the knob turns, as strongly as the head unit asks"
    default y
    depends on WSKNOB_HAPTIC
    help
      The head unit answers each turn it acts on with a strength: volume
      gets stronger towards 100 %, temperature, seat and fan towards their
      ends, map zoom towards its limits, and the radio with the signal of
      the station tuned. The motor is driven in real-time mode at an
      amplitude between WSKNOB_HAPTIC_TURN_MIN and _MAX for
      WSKNOB_HAPTIC_TURN_MS, and stops. A turn the head unit does nothing
      with, such as scrolling a list, has no tick.

config WSKNOB_HAPTIC_TURN_MIN
    int "Amplitude of the lightest tick (of 127)"
    range 1 127
    default 40
    depends on WSKNOB_HAPTIC_TURN
    help
      What strength 1 drives the motor at. Too low and an ERM does not get
      going in the time a tick lasts, so the lightest ticks are not felt.

config WSKNOB_HAPTIC_TURN_MAX
    int "Amplitude of the strongest tick (of 127)"
    range 1 127
    default 127
    depends on WSKNOB_HAPTIC_TURN

config WSKNOB_HAPTIC_TURN_MS
    int "How long one tick drives the motor (ms)"
    range 4 100
    default 25
    depends on WSKNOB_HAPTIC_TURN
    help
      Each detent restarts it, so turning fast feels like one buzz at the
      current strength, and the motor stops this long after the last
      detent the head unit acted on.

comment "Ring"

config WSKNOB_SCREEN_RING
    bool "Draw the head unit's LED ring round the edge of the display"
    default y
    help
      This board has no LED ring, so the five colours the head unit sends
      30 times a second would be lost. With this set they are drawn as a
      band round the outside of the display, blended between the five
      model LEDs so a pattern that points somewhere still points there,
      and the face is drawn inside it. Without it the ring frames are
      dropped and the face fills the display.

config WSKNOB_SCREEN_RING_PX
    int "Width of the on-screen ring (px)"
    range 6 40
    default 16
    depends on WSKNOB_SCREEN_RING
    help
      Measured in from the edge of the 360 px display. The face is drawn
      in the rest.

endmenu
